The outline is the producer's proposed hypothesis of how this scenario reaches the hazard, not an observed result. Each node line gives the node ID, bracketed source IDs, the category and details in parentheses, and the label; a child line starts with "-" or, under an ordered AND, its position, and the other indented lines describe the node above them. AND means every child must hold; "AND in order" also means the children happen in the listed order. OR means any one child is enough. The line of other scenarios that reach the same hazard is not part of this test. You may cite a node ID or a bracketed source ID in interpretation.source_refs.
